# Every change requires review from @In-My-Head.
#
# Pages on my.mcleanbible.org load this repo's JS, CSS and Liquid templates
# straight from GitHub Pages, in the same origin that holds MinistryPlatform
# login tokens. Anything merged to main is live script on those pages, so the
# `require-secret-scan` ruleset on main requires an approving code-owner review.
# Admins can bypass the review via pull request so the owner can merge their own
# work (GitHub does not allow approving your own PR); direct pushes stay blocked.
#
# Adding staff later: give them write access (so they can push branches and open
# PRs) and leave this file alone. Only add a second owner here if you want that
# person's review to satisfy the requirement on its own.

*                   @In-My-Head

# Called out explicitly so they stay owned even if the catch-all changes.
**/*.js             @In-My-Head
**/Template/**      @In-My-Head
/.github/           @In-My-Head
